                ("Recognising Account Takeover", "Account takeover occurs when an unauthorised person gains control of an account. Signs can include unfamiliar logins, changed recovery information, unexpected messages, new devices or password-reset notices.", "If takeover is suspected, use the legitimate service to change the password, revoke unfamiliar sessions where supported, enable MFA and review recovery settings. Contact the service through its official support channel if access has been lost.", "Friends report receiving strange messages from a learner's social account. The learner checks active sessions, changes the password from the official app and removes unfamiliar sessions.", "Treat unfamiliar activity seriously; secure the account through official controls; warn contacts if malicious messages were sent."),
